   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/Idempotents/Primitive/Top.lean",
   "fix": "Export the two covers: `IsIndecomposableModule.isProjectiveCover_of_surjective` \u2014 for `[IsSemiprimaryRing R]`, indecomposable projective `P`, simple `M` and surjective `f : P \u2192\u2097[R] M`, `IsProjectiveCover f` (from `ker_eq_jacobson_smul_top_of_surjective` plus `isSuperfluous_smul_top_of_isNilpotent`); and its `Ae` specialization taking `IsIdempotentElem e` and discharging projectivity internally, e.g. `isProjectiveCover_mkQ_jacobson_smul_top_span_singleton (he : IsIdempotentElem e) [IsSemiprimaryRing A] : IsProjectiveCover (Ring.jacobson A \u2022 (\u22a4 : Submodule A \u21a5(Ideal.span {e}))).mkQ`.",
   "issue": "The module docstring and the PR description claim `Ae \u21a0 Ae / J(Ae)` is identified as a projective cover, but no declaration in the PR states `IsProjectiveCover` for `Ae` or for a surjection from an indecomposable projective onto a simple module. `grep IsProjectiveCover TauCeti/RingTheory` matches only the docstring line, and the new `isProjectiveCover_mkQ_smul_top_of_isNilpotent` has no in-repo use. It also cannot be applied to `Ae` by instance search: `Module.Projective A \u21a5(Ideal.span {e})` is supplied only by the theorem `IsIdempotentElem.projective_span_singleton` (Idempotents/Module.lean:104), not an instance, so every consumer must re-derive it.",
   "line": 23
